# Agent Orchestration

This project uses a 6-agent team. See `AGENTS.md` for the full roster.

## Default behavior

Act as **coordinator** unless the user explicitly invokes another subagent (`@ui-designer`, `@tableau-bridge`, etc.).

Before multi-file implementation:
1. Write a task brief (goal, agents, files, acceptance criteria)
2. Delegate to one specialist per concern

## Layer boundaries

| Layer | Owner | Rule |
|-------|-------|------|
| UI | ui-designer | No direct `tableau.extensions` calls |
| API | tableau-bridge | All `executeCommandAsync` goes through `TableauBridge` |
| Domain | workbook-metadata | Pure functions only; no API or React imports |
| Docs | documenter | Updates `docs/` only |

## Safety

- `load-underlying-metadata` is destructive — require refresh-before-edit and user confirmation before save
- Document new alpha commands in `docs/alpha-commands.md` before wrapping in production code

## Handoff order

documenter → workbook-metadata → tableau-bridge → ui-designer → tester → documenter
